## Final Judgement
## Summary

The evidence from multiple reputable sources is consistent and conclusive. The viral video does not show an attack on the French embassy in Sudan. Instead, it depicts the September 2012 attack on the **German embassy** in Khartoum, Sudan (along with the US and UK embassies), carried out by protesters angered by the "Innocence of Muslims" film. Multiple fact-checking organizations (BoomLive, Factly) have independently confirmed through reverse image searches and cross-referencing with 2012 news reports that the building shown being set on fire is the German embassy, not the French embassy. No attack on the French embassy in Sudan occurred in late October 2020; the video was falsely recirculated in the wake of protests related to French President Macron's comments on Islam following the beheading of teacher Samuel Paty.

